1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,643
He doesn't play monsters.

2
00:00:01,643 --> 00:00:02,695
He lets them in.

3
00:00:02,695 --> 00:00:05,389
August seventeenth, nineteen forty-three.

4
00:00:05,389 --> 00:00:06,047
Manhattan.

5
00:00:06,047 --> 00:00:10,910
A boy born between two painters who had already begun to leave each other.

6
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:17,745
That boy will become one of the most watched faces in cinema, and the man who almost never explains why.

7
00:00:17,745 --> 00:00:19,257
This is Robert De Niro.

8
00:00:19,257 --> 00:00:20,506
Not the impression.

9
00:00:20,506 --> 00:00:21,820
The life underneath.

10
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:25,302
The father, Robert De Niro Senior, was a painter.

11
00:00:25,302 --> 00:00:26,885
An abstract expressionist.

12
00:00:26,885 --> 00:00:28,650
He studied with Hans Hofmann.

13
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:30,354
Peggy Guggenheim showed him.

14
00:00:30,354 --> 00:00:37,535
In nineteen forty-six he had a solo show at Art of This Century, the room where New York was about to change painting.

15
00:00:37,535 --> 00:00:40,091
The mother, Virginia Admiral, painted too.

16
00:00:40,091 --> 00:00:43,134
Then she mostly stopped, and she raised the child.

17
00:00:43,134 --> 00:00:46,299
The marriage, from nineteen forty-two, did not hold.

18
00:00:46,299 --> 00:00:48,794
They separated when Robert was about two.

19
00:00:48,794 --> 00:00:53,237
The father became a man you sometimes caught on the street, on a bicycle.

20
00:00:53,237 --> 00:00:54,820
A second, and he was gone.

21
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:59,445
Years later De Niro said the sentence that explains more than any interview.

22
00:00:59,445 --> 00:01:01,210
My father was the real thing.

23
00:01:01,210 --> 00:01:02,732
The father kept journals.

24
00:01:02,732 --> 00:01:04,131
In them, a private war.

25
00:01:04,131 --> 00:01:09,609
He was gay, in a world that punished that truth, and he wrote it down by hand, with guilt.

26
00:01:09,609 --> 00:01:12,469
The son did not grow up inside that confession.

27
00:01:12,469 --> 00:01:14,295
He grew up beside the silence.

28
00:01:14,295 --> 00:01:20,625
In twenty fourteen he produced the documentary Remembering the Artist and read those journals on camera.

29
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:25,676
The man who never talks opened, because the paintings had not been given their due.

30
00:01:25,676 --> 00:01:28,537
He said he wanted his father to have his place.

31
00:01:28,537 --> 00:01:30,423
That it was his responsibility.

32
00:01:30,423 --> 00:01:40,100
When the father was dying of cancer, in nineteen ninety-three, on the day he turned seventy-one, it was the mother, decades divorced from him, who took him in.

33
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:43,326
The son was already the most feared actor in America.

34
00:01:43,326 --> 00:01:47,160
He was still the boy who had watched a bicycle turn the corner.

35
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:50,068
Robert junior was not an easy student.

36
00:01:50,068 --> 00:01:52,160
School slipped through his hands.

37
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:59,195
He left high school at sixteen to study the only thing that held him: watching people until he could wear them.

38
00:01:59,195 --> 00:02:05,279
Stella Adler taught him that the actor's job is to imagine the life, not to beg for the emotion.

39
00:02:05,279 --> 00:02:09,398
Later, Lee Strasberg and the Actors Studio pushed the other door.

40
00:02:09,398 --> 00:02:09,842
Memory.

41
00:02:09,842 --> 00:02:10,222
Nerve.

42
00:02:10,222 --> 00:02:11,870
What is actually at stake.

43
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:16,053
De Niro took both schools and then did something less fashionable.

44
00:02:16,053 --> 00:02:17,320
He did the homework.

45
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,018
The accent.

46
00:02:18,018 --> 00:02:19,475
The weight of the body.

47
00:02:19,475 --> 00:02:21,250
The way a man holds a glass.

48
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:23,912
He has never liked the myth of possession.

49
00:02:23,912 --> 00:02:24,989
He likes choices.

50
00:02:24,989 --> 00:02:25,876
Concrete ones.

51
00:02:25,876 --> 00:02:28,348
The kind you can repeat on take twelve.

52
00:02:28,348 --> 00:02:30,756
His early films do not ask permission.

53
00:02:30,756 --> 00:02:36,651
With Brian De Palma he makes Greetings and Hi, Mom!, strange satires of Vietnam-era New York.

54
00:02:36,651 --> 00:02:40,009
In nineteen seventy-three comes Bang the Drum Slowly.

55
00:02:40,009 --> 00:02:42,038
He plays a catcher who is dying.

56
00:02:42,038 --> 00:02:43,432
The business looks up.

57
00:02:43,432 --> 00:02:46,981
The same year, Martin Scorsese puts him in Mean Streets.

58
00:02:46,981 --> 00:02:47,678
Johnny Boy.

59
00:02:47,678 --> 00:02:51,608
A neighborhood fuse, in Little Italy, smiling as he lights it.

60
00:02:51,608 --> 00:02:53,572
Scorsese was not hiring a star.

61
00:02:53,572 --> 00:02:55,220
He was hiring a frequency.

62
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,833
Then Francis Ford Coppola asks for the impossible.

63
00:02:58,833 --> 00:03:02,693
Play Vito Corleone as a young man, in The Godfather, Part Two.

64
00:03:02,693 --> 00:03:05,246
Without doing a Marlon Brando impression.

65
00:03:05,246 --> 00:03:07,612
Without sharing the frame with Brando.

66
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:09,417
They shot their halves apart.

67
00:03:09,417 --> 00:03:15,395
De Niro learned the Sicilian dialect until the lines sat in his mouth like a language from home.

68
00:03:15,395 --> 00:03:20,002
He watched Brando the way a painter studies a canvas from across the room.

69
00:03:20,002 --> 00:03:21,372
Not to copy the brush.

70
00:03:21,372 --> 00:03:22,928
To understand the weight.

71
00:03:22,928 --> 00:03:24,298
Nineteen seventy-five.

72
00:03:24,298 --> 00:03:26,539
The Oscar for Best Supporting Actor.

73
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:27,660
He was thirty-one.

74
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:29,528
He did not look like a winner.

75
00:03:29,528 --> 00:03:34,820
He looked like a man who had borrowed someone else's youth and returned it undamaged.

76
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:36,672
Nineteen seventy-six.

77
00:03:36,672 --> 00:03:37,445
Taxi Driver.

78
00:03:37,445 --> 00:03:44,593
Paul Schrader writes Travis Bickle, an insomniac in a metal coffin, rolling through a city that has come apart.

79
00:03:44,593 --> 00:03:45,687
Scorsese directs.

80
00:03:45,687 --> 00:03:53,157
De Niro shaves a mohawk, puts on the fatigue jacket, and builds a man so lonely he rehearses friendship in a mirror.

81
00:03:53,157 --> 00:03:54,316
You talkin' to me?

82
00:03:54,316 --> 00:03:55,604
The line was a seed.

83
00:03:55,604 --> 00:04:01,528
He grew the whole interrogation, asking an empty room a question no one was going to answer.

84
00:04:01,528 --> 00:04:03,846
Cannes gave the film the Palme d'Or.

85
00:04:03,846 --> 00:04:05,971
America gave it a permanent echo.

86
00:04:05,971 --> 00:04:08,032
People quote Travis like a joke.

87
00:04:08,032 --> 00:04:09,963
The performance is not a joke.

88
00:04:09,963 --> 00:04:15,244
It is a diagnosis of a city, and of the kind of man that city keeps manufacturing.

89
00:04:15,244 --> 00:04:18,270
On that shoot, Diahnne Abbott has a small role.

90
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:19,944
They marry that same year.

91
00:04:19,944 --> 00:04:20,975
Raphael is born.

92
00:04:20,975 --> 00:04:23,550
De Niro adopts Abbott's daughter, Drena.

93
00:04:23,550 --> 00:04:29,925
For a while, the most isolated character in American movies is, off camera, a husband and a father.

94
00:04:29,925 --> 00:04:38,425
He also shoots Bertolucci's Nineteen Hundred, and the next year Scorsese's difficult musical New York, New York, with Liza Minnelli.

95
00:04:38,425 --> 00:04:39,520
It was not a hit.

96
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:44,800
De Niro had already stopped letting the box office decide which performance stays.

97
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:48,472
If Taxi Driver was a nerve, Raging Bull was a body.

98
00:04:48,472 --> 00:04:49,281
Jake LaMotta.

99
00:04:49,281 --> 00:04:51,084
Jealousy as a fighting style.

100
00:04:51,084 --> 00:04:54,008
Scorsese did not want to make a boxing picture.

101
00:04:54,008 --> 00:04:56,185
De Niro kept bringing him the book.

102
00:04:56,185 --> 00:05:01,409
When they finally shot it, in black and white, he did what the legend still resists.

103
00:05:01,409 --> 00:05:03,710
First he played the fighter in shape.

104
00:05:03,710 --> 00:05:09,557
Then he shut the production down and gained about sixty pounds to play the older, ruined Jake.

105
00:05:09,557 --> 00:05:10,241
Not a suit.

106
00:05:10,241 --> 00:05:14,844
A decision, lived for months, so the camera would have nothing to forgive.

107
00:05:14,844 --> 00:05:16,088
Nineteen eighty-one.

108
00:05:16,088 --> 00:05:17,643
The Oscar for Best Actor.

109
00:05:17,643 --> 00:05:20,255
People who agree on nothing agree on this.

110
00:05:20,255 --> 00:05:23,925
It is one of the great performances in the history of film.

111
00:05:23,925 --> 00:05:28,963
In the last scene Jake is alone, shadowboxing, rehearsing, badly, how to be seen.

112
00:05:28,963 --> 00:05:30,207
The monster is gone.

113
00:05:30,207 --> 00:05:32,197
A man is left practicing a line.

114
00:05:32,197 --> 00:05:35,493
Before that, The Deer Hunter, nineteen seventy-eight.

115
00:05:35,493 --> 00:05:40,594
Steel country, Vietnam, a wedding long enough to show you what the war will break.

116
00:05:40,594 --> 00:05:41,775
Another nomination.

117
00:05:41,775 --> 00:05:44,388
His character does not explain the damage.

118
00:05:44,388 --> 00:05:45,321
He swallows it.

119
00:05:45,321 --> 00:05:48,244
And in nineteen eighty-two, The King of Comedy.

120
00:05:48,244 --> 00:05:51,354
Rupert Pupkin, the fan who decides to kidnap fame.

121
00:05:51,354 --> 00:05:52,349
People hated it.

122
00:05:52,349 --> 00:05:53,842
Time made it a prophecy.

123
00:05:53,842 --> 00:05:59,999
In twenty nineteen, in Joker, De Niro steps through the mirror and plays the host, Murray Franklin.

124
00:05:59,999 --> 00:06:03,420
Yesterday's stalker is now the man with the microphone.

125
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:09,289
The eighties and nineties are a map of American unease, and he is at the crossroads.

126
00:06:09,289 --> 00:06:12,165
Once Upon a Time in America, by Sergio Leone.

127
00:06:12,165 --> 00:06:18,877
The Untouchables: his Al Capone walks into a banquet with a baseball bat and ends a conversation forever.

128
00:06:18,877 --> 00:06:23,415
The Mission, with Jeremy Irons: a man hauling his guilt up a waterfall.

129
00:06:23,415 --> 00:06:27,761
Brazil, by Terry Gilliam, where he lets himself be physically funny.

130
00:06:27,761 --> 00:06:31,213
Midnight Run: a bounty hunter opposite Charles Grodin.

131
00:06:31,213 --> 00:06:35,240
The face, it turns out, can be funny without asking permission.

132
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,029
Goodfellas, nineteen ninety.

133
00:06:37,029 --> 00:06:37,860
Jimmy Conway.

134
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:41,248
King of the neighborhood, and the smile is a warning.

135
00:06:41,248 --> 00:06:46,170
The same year, Awakenings, a doctor beside patients the world had filed away.

136
00:06:46,170 --> 00:06:47,384
Another nomination.

137
00:06:47,384 --> 00:06:49,685
Cape Fear: Max Cady, ink and threat.

138
00:06:49,685 --> 00:06:50,899
Another nomination.

139
00:06:50,899 --> 00:07:00,231
In nineteen ninety-three he directs for the first time, A Bronx Tale, and plays a father trying to pull his son off the false shine of the street.

140
00:07:00,231 --> 00:07:02,149
The neighborhood is not a set.

141
00:07:02,149 --> 00:07:04,450
It is the language of his childhood.

142
00:07:04,950 --> 00:07:06,326
Nineteen ninety-five.

143
00:07:06,326 --> 00:07:06,719
Twice.

144
00:07:06,719 --> 00:07:08,554
Casino, with Scorsese again.

145
00:07:08,554 --> 00:07:11,830
Ace Rothstein, convinced he can manage the desert.

146
00:07:11,830 --> 00:07:13,533
And Heat, by Michael Mann.

147
00:07:13,533 --> 00:07:16,679
Neil McCauley, a thief with a monk's discipline.

148
00:07:16,679 --> 00:07:18,644
Al Pacino is across the table.

149
00:07:18,644 --> 00:07:23,231
They had shared The Godfather, Part Two, without ever sharing a scene.

150
00:07:23,231 --> 00:07:27,424
In a Los Angeles diner, two decades of myth sit down for coffee.

151
00:07:27,424 --> 00:07:28,669
Neither one blinks.

152
00:07:28,669 --> 00:07:29,914
The scene is quiet.

153
00:07:29,914 --> 00:07:31,552
That is why it detonates.

154
00:07:31,552 --> 00:07:38,956
At the turn of the century, the man who had been America's unease agrees to be America's difficult father-in-law.

155
00:07:38,956 --> 00:07:40,070
Meet the Parents.

156
00:07:40,070 --> 00:07:40,856
Jack Byrnes.

157
00:07:40,856 --> 00:07:44,722
A polygraph in the basement and a smile like a locked door.

158
00:07:44,722 --> 00:07:46,426
The movie is a phenomenon.

159
00:07:46,426 --> 00:07:50,357
People who never saw Raging Bull now do the stare at dinner.

160
00:07:50,357 --> 00:07:52,192
He does not become a mascot.

161
00:07:52,192 --> 00:07:54,878
He proves control is also a comic weapon.

162
00:07:54,878 --> 00:07:57,892
In Analyze This, the gangster goes to therapy.

163
00:07:57,892 --> 00:08:03,724
In Silver Linings Playbook, twenty twelve, he is a superstitious father, suddenly tender.

164
00:08:03,724 --> 00:08:04,969
Another nomination.

165
00:08:04,969 --> 00:08:08,573
He researches the comedy the way he researches a crime.

166
00:08:08,573 --> 00:08:14,535
And in two thousand six he directs The Good Shepherd, a cold film about the birth of the C.

167
00:08:14,535 --> 00:08:14,666
I.

168
00:08:14,666 --> 00:08:14,797
A.

169
00:08:14,797 --> 00:08:15,846
The old subject.

170
00:08:15,846 --> 00:08:18,270
What a life of secrets does to a man.

171
00:08:18,770 --> 00:08:21,447
Off the set, the biography is not a poster.

172
00:08:21,447 --> 00:08:23,563
It is a family with several doors.

173
00:08:23,563 --> 00:08:27,360
The marriage to Diahnne Abbott ends in nineteen eighty-eight.

174
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:33,211
With Toukie Smith he has twins in nineteen ninety-five, Julian and Airyn, through a surrogate.

175
00:08:33,211 --> 00:08:37,817
In April twenty twenty-five, Airyn speaks publicly as a transgender woman.

176
00:08:37,817 --> 00:08:40,058
De Niro's answer is short and clear.

177
00:08:40,058 --> 00:08:41,054
He supports her.

178
00:08:41,054 --> 00:08:42,859
He loves her as his daughter.

179
00:08:42,859 --> 00:08:43,481
No speech.

180
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:44,975
A father, on the record.

181
00:08:44,975 --> 00:08:48,212
He marries Grace Hightower in nineteen ninety-seven.

182
00:08:48,212 --> 00:08:50,142
Elliot is born in ninety-eight.

183
00:08:50,142 --> 00:08:54,063
Helen Grace arrives in twenty eleven, also through a surrogate.

184
00:08:54,063 --> 00:08:56,117
They separate in twenty eighteen.

185
00:08:56,117 --> 00:08:59,603
He asks for privacy and keeps the sentence that matters.

186
00:08:59,603 --> 00:09:02,964
They will go on as partners in raising their children.

187
00:09:02,964 --> 00:09:06,325
Around twenty twenty-one he is seen with Tiffany Chen.

188
00:09:06,325 --> 00:09:10,745
On April sixth, twenty twenty-three, Gia Virginia Chen-De Niro is born.

189
00:09:10,745 --> 00:09:13,732
He is seventy-nine, and he does not announce it.

190
00:09:13,732 --> 00:09:16,782
A month later an interviewer counts six children.

191
00:09:16,782 --> 00:09:18,090
De Niro corrects him.

192
00:09:18,090 --> 00:09:19,085
Seven, actually.

193
00:09:19,085 --> 00:09:20,206
I just had a baby.

194
00:09:20,206 --> 00:09:24,688
He has said that when he looks at Gia, what is consuming him goes quiet.

195
00:09:24,688 --> 00:09:28,547
He wants her to grow up with Chinese and English in the house.

196
00:09:28,547 --> 00:09:29,480
Seven children.

197
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:33,091
More than fifty years between the oldest and the youngest.

198
00:09:33,091 --> 00:09:34,584
Drena became an actress.

199
00:09:34,584 --> 00:09:37,385
Raphael built a life in New York real estate.

200
00:09:37,385 --> 00:09:41,431
The others grew up under a last name that arrives before they do.

201
00:09:41,431 --> 00:09:43,610
He does not pretend that is simple.

202
00:09:44,110 --> 00:09:45,661
There is another De Niro.

203
00:09:45,661 --> 00:09:48,268
The one who builds rooms for other people.

204
00:09:48,268 --> 00:09:51,867
With the chef Nobu Matsuhisa he becomes a partner in Nobu.

205
00:09:51,867 --> 00:09:54,225
The first restaurant opens in Tribeca.

206
00:09:54,225 --> 00:09:57,390
Downtown stops being only a location in his movies.

207
00:09:57,390 --> 00:09:58,569
It becomes a table.

208
00:09:58,569 --> 00:10:00,183
A bet on the neighborhood.

209
00:10:00,183 --> 00:10:03,285
With Jane Rosenthal he founds Tribeca Productions.

210
00:10:03,285 --> 00:10:12,842
After September eleventh, two thousand one, when the dust in lower Manhattan was not a metaphor, they create the Tribeca Film Festival with Craig Hatkoff.

211
00:10:12,842 --> 00:10:14,456
A festival as a civic act.

212
00:10:14,456 --> 00:10:15,821
Bring the lights back.

213
00:10:15,821 --> 00:10:18,738
Bring the audiences back south of Canal Street.

214
00:10:18,738 --> 00:10:22,833
He has never been the most sentimental New Yorker at a microphone.

215
00:10:22,833 --> 00:10:24,323
He did something harder.

216
00:10:24,323 --> 00:10:24,943
He stayed.

217
00:10:24,943 --> 00:10:25,750
And he built.

218
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:29,272
The late performances refuse an easy victory lap.

219
00:10:29,272 --> 00:10:31,122
The Irishman, twenty nineteen.

220
00:10:31,122 --> 00:10:33,034
Scorsese again, now on Netflix.

221
00:10:33,034 --> 00:10:41,051
The digital de-aging works here as a moral instrument: a face moving backward into the crimes, then forward into the nursing home.

222
00:10:41,051 --> 00:10:43,764
Frank Sheeran confuses loyalty with erasure.

223
00:10:43,764 --> 00:10:44,875
Joe Pesci returns.

224
00:10:44,875 --> 00:10:46,231
Pacino is Jimmy Hoffa.

225
00:10:46,231 --> 00:10:48,575
De Niro is the silence after the shot.

226
00:10:48,575 --> 00:10:49,747
Another nomination.

227
00:10:49,747 --> 00:10:52,707
Killers of the Flower Moon, twenty twenty-three.

228
00:10:52,707 --> 00:10:58,319
William Hale, the uncle who smiles while a people are killed for the oil under their names.

229
00:10:58,319 --> 00:11:00,107
Politeness, used as a weapon.

230
00:11:00,107 --> 00:11:06,459
Half a century after Mean Streets, they are still asking what a man will justify in the name of family.

231
00:11:06,459 --> 00:11:07,631
Another nomination.

232
00:11:07,631 --> 00:11:08,309
Two Oscars.

233
00:11:08,309 --> 00:11:09,419
A pile of almosts.

234
00:11:09,419 --> 00:11:12,380
He never acted as if the almosts were the point.

235
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:19,225
In twenty twenty-five he plays two mobsters in one body, Frank Costello and Vito Genovese, in The Alto Knights.

236
00:11:19,225 --> 00:11:28,291
And in Zero Day, his first series as the lead, he is a former president called back because the country does not understand the attack it suffered.

237
00:11:28,291 --> 00:11:32,731
That May, at Cannes, Leonardo DiCaprio hands him an honorary Palme d'Or.

238
00:11:32,731 --> 00:11:34,951
De Niro does not talk about himself.

239
00:11:34,951 --> 00:11:43,893
He talks about art as a public act, about a democracy he believes has to be defended, and about a tariff on films made outside the United States.

240
00:11:43,893 --> 00:11:44,818
Agree or don't.

241
00:11:44,818 --> 00:11:49,320
He showed up, and he used the microphone for something other than thanks.

242
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:53,144
In August twenty twenty-six, Netflix releases The Whisper Man.

243
00:11:53,144 --> 00:12:03,381
He is Peter Willis, a retired detective and a father called back because children are disappearing, and because his son, played by Adam Scott, has no one else to ask.

244
00:12:03,381 --> 00:12:09,980
At eighty-three he is still who they write when the story needs someone who knows where the body is buried.

245
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:13,039
So what do you do with a life like that.

246
00:12:13,039 --> 00:12:14,575
You can list the movies.

247
00:12:14,575 --> 00:12:14,894
Vito.

248
00:12:14,894 --> 00:12:15,342
Travis.

249
00:12:15,342 --> 00:12:15,662
Jake.

250
00:12:15,662 --> 00:12:16,110
Capone.

251
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:16,942
Jimmy Conway.

252
00:12:16,942 --> 00:12:17,837
Neil McCauley.

253
00:12:17,837 --> 00:12:18,605
Jack Byrnes.

254
00:12:18,605 --> 00:12:19,501
Frank Sheeran.

255
00:12:19,501 --> 00:12:20,332
William Hale.

256
00:12:20,332 --> 00:12:21,996
The list is the easy part.

257
00:12:21,996 --> 00:12:29,801
The hard part is the boy on a Greenwich Village street who learned, early, that love can be a bicycle going the other way.

258
00:12:29,801 --> 00:12:34,216
He spent sixty years learning how to stand still inside other people.

259
00:12:34,216 --> 00:12:36,327
Killers, comics, fathers, frauds.

260
00:12:36,327 --> 00:12:40,293
Precisely enough that we forget there is an actor in the room.

261
00:12:40,293 --> 00:12:42,213
He doesn't interpret the dark.

262
00:12:42,213 --> 00:12:44,836
He opens the door and does not step back.

263
00:12:44,836 --> 00:12:46,947
Robert De Niro is still watching.

264
00:12:46,947 --> 00:12:49,890
And he still does not owe you the explanation.
